proposal.detail:
Structure (verified 2023-2026): 120 p in total. Part 1 is one 20 p task, part 2 two 20 p tasks, part 3 two 30 p tasks. In parts 2 and 3, content points (counted by perspectives and examples, on a 3/6/9 or 4/7/10/13 ladder) are scored separately from information processing (concepts, application, analysis, evaluation, argumentation, structure).

Deductions:
- irrelevant content, up to 5 p;
- many small errors, up to 3 or 5 p;
- one fundamental error, up to 5 or 8 p;
- not referring to the material, 3-5 p;
- going over the character limit.
Length alone earns nothing.

TE2 content seen in YTL papers:
- s1: research-type definitions (2023 autumn); survey vs register data (2023 autumn); results tables (FinTerveys tooth brushing, 2024 autumn); turning tables into charts plus a WHO-areas measures task (2025 spring); cognitive biases with fictional people (2025 autumn).
- s2: an advert's reliability (2025 autumn); ethical analysis of a chatbot answer (2025 spring); home tests and health competence (2025 spring); social media and loneliness from accounts and a video (2023 autumn).
- s3-s4: radon without material (2024 spring); sustainable development's four dimensions without material (2025 autumn); clean water (2024 autumn); noise and the Ottawa model (2023 autumn); Health in All Policies from an e-scooter text (2026 spring).
- s7-s8: dependence, 30 p with two materials (2024 autumn, spot-checked). It required forms, mechanisms (biological, psychological, social), features (tolerance, withdrawal, loss of control, relapse) and harms that are direct and indirect, for the individual, community and society.
- s5 and s6: no direct task found in the papers read.

What TE2 must therefore carry:
- precise concepts with health examples;
- reading and charting tables;
- judging data origin and reliability;
- spotting persuasion;
- ethical perspectives;
- WHO health-promotion areas and Health in All Policies as frames for measures;
- the dependence model above.
Each topic practises all three task sizes, and the mix across the module includes concept tasks without material.

Caveats: brief 003's coverage matrix is missing, so module shares of exam points are unknown. Spring 2023 and earlier were not read. Exam tasks for te2-07 and te2-08 are model-only. The point ladders need review by the human teacher reviewer.
